r betraying marco and on a  distant planet beyond the rings a new  power begins to rise this mostly matches  up with the talking points that they  brought to the comic-con panel which  i've already discussed in the other  video but i thought it's worth looking  at here because it does add context to  everything we see  the teaser opens with holden pushing a  button which i sincerely hope is a nod  to one of my favorite lines in the books  he's on the rossi he's sitting in the  pilot's chair and he yells everyone  brace and then you see the drive light  up one thing you don't see in this  trailer is bull and it's not clear  what's happening here it's very unlikely  that holden would be taking over the  piloting duties for alex since that's  not something he knows how to do this is  probably an emergency and we see  everyone's in suits and if all these  shots are connected then we see the  others hitting the deck there's a quick  shot of the rossi doing maneuvers with a  lot of pdc fire and then it cuts to the  tynan getting lit up with drummer in a  suit in the pilot's chair there's this  shot where you can see that the hull has  a lot of holes blown through it and what  looks like drummer slumped over in the  chair i highly doubt that this is the  end of her story if for no other reason  then why would they show that in the  opening seconds of a quick teaser it's  almost as if they want you to believe  that the rossi found themselves in a  situation where it was her or them and  to me it all feels like misdirection  what you can take away from this for  sure is that there are going to be some  exciting space battles and it looks like  everyone will be involved after that  there's a shot of earth in new york city  you can see the sky is dark there's  smoke rising from the skyline and that  most of the city is still underwater  from the sea walls failing in season  five after the rocks hit you hear abba  sarah say we're broken trying  desperately to keep ourselves going by  pretending we're not we see her looking  at a data pad sitting there deep in  thought holding a naomi strapping in and  a shot of amos thinking wearing a suit  and turning to look at the rasanante  plaque that's cut with her continuing  saying that we must remember the lives  we've lost  so in the comic-con panel they mentioned  that the earth had been totally  obliterated by the free navy's asteroid  attack that part wasn't really clear at  the end of last season after nancy gal's  death abasarallah is back in charge and  that means that she's gonna be dealing  with the aftermath there's a scene here  where she's walking into a room with un  body bags stacked on top of each other  and then a sequence with bobby taking  fire in her power armor and from the sky  overhead it looks like she's in the slow  zone and then a shot of clarissa  grimacing grabbing her head on the rossi  and you see that the voice over is  coming from abu sarah talking to someone  on the surface of earth so the first  half is bullets flying the earth dying  and most of the characters sitting  around thinking looking like they're on  the verge of crying we transitioned to  the second half with a quick burst of  action shots there's more space battle  shots with the pella firing torpedoes an  explosion that looks like it's on a  station those continued asteroid attacks  on earth from orbit from the free navy  and then the focus shifts to marco who  we know is responsible for all of this  chaos from the graffiti you get the idea  that some of the belters are getting  behind him and then there's this shot on  series where it looks like he's getting  ready to address a crowd who seemed to  be cheering him on you see him hand fill  up a gun and then in a different shot he  says you and i were meant to be out here  in the darkness in the fight that's who  we were born to be while he's talking we  see them at their battle stations on the  pela and then another sequence of  drummer firing a gun then there's a  couple of intriguing shots from laconia  you get a much better look at the  orbital platforms that were left behind  from the gate builders we saw those in  the closing moments of season five and  here again you can't miss that blue glow  inside after that we see a young girl  walking and it's through the lens that  resembles some of the shots from season  four that involve the investigator and  the final shot is the rossi spinning  with its point defense cannons firing on  something that explodes nearly engulfing  the ship there was a shot earlier that  looked like rocks flying through space  and i think that might be what they're  shooting at here from what we see it  looks like the current conflict is going  to be taking a toll on everyone and  they'll be dealing with it or acting out  because of it in different ways marco's  coming off his biggest victory at the  end of last season and this makes it  looks like he starts out riding high  there's a lot we don't see here it's a  pretty tight focus on the core  characters which we mostly know where  they are a lot of the questions i have  about how this season's going to develop  come more from the characters outside  the inner circle like i said earlier  there's no bull in this we don't see any  monika there's really no shots of bobby  on the rossi instead we see her on earth  with abasarala and then later in the  slow zone and with fred johnson missing  there's really not much representation  for the belt outside of drummer who  really doesn't have any power at this  point marco can hold on to his gains if  earth is on the defensive but he has to  have allies to maintain order which  means we might meet a lot of new  characters  just to reiterate some of the details  from yesterday's video it has been  confirmed that there are only six  episodes in this final season the only  one they mentioned being longer than  usual was the finale with a run time of  65 minutes they're only doing book six  nothing from the final trilogy and then  they're adding some stuff on laconia  that comes from the novella strange dogs  i read an article in collider today  where ty frank was talking about it and  he said i think the thing that season  six does is it pays off the story that  we began in episode one of season one  where the martians the earthers and the  belters were all in this incredibly  uneasy and unstable political system  with the belters absolutely being the  foot of that table and everyone fighting  for their place in the solar system i  think we pay off that story in a very  satisfying way and we keep some of the  mystery intact involving the greater  forces of the universe that humans are  only starting to become aware if we want  to tell more stories there were a lot of  comments on my video with people who  were worried about the short season  which i get but just remember they did  do book three and seven normal length  episodes in the third season admittedly  i thought some of that felt rushed but  there's actually less to adapt from the  sixth book because of what they already  covered in season five i do think it's  doable and if they really nail it it  could turn out to be exhilarating i  think what people might find more  troubling is that part of his comment  talking about the greater forces of the  universe some people are going to be  pissed that there's no conclusion to the  gate builders and unknown aggressors  part of the story that is what it is i  mean they took three additional novels  to get into that and there's really no  number of episodes that you could tack  on to the end of this season to make  that work if we want to see that we just  have to hope that there'll be more  expanse in the future it's weird because  you can never really tell why they're  saying what they're saying when they  talk about things like the pause or if  they're throwing it out there if we want  to tell more stories you can't tell if  they're doing that because they have  something planned that they can't reveal  or if they're just doing that to try to  make it happen as a fan i tend to think  that there's something going on but then  i kind of have to pull myself back you  know i don't really know i just want to  see that stuff to this point i can say  that they've made hints but they've  definitely not confirmed anything and  that's really all there is to it a  couple other details the first episode  and only the first episode will premiere  on december 10th then they're going to  be released weekly which means that the  finale will air on january 14th so the  end of the expanse is coming and i think  that brings us to the end of this video  as well one more thing before i go i'm  not sure how i feel about this situation  where there's tension building with the  crew of the rossi i kind of see where  they're going but it also kind of feels  wrong in their last hurrah you know so  i'm interested to hear what you guys  think about that and how big of a part  of the season you think it'll turn out  to be so let me know in the comments  what you think about the teaser what you  think about all these announcements what  was your favorite shot and if you want  to talk book spoilers i'm all for it  just make sure you mark those so we  don't spoil it for everyone else please  like this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon

